      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Talks of a railroad through Sac County began in 1859, but the first tracks reached Sac City only in 1879.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sac_City%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1908, Sac City built its Chautauqua Pavilion, the only surviving Chautauqua building in Iowa, which still hosts community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
